WEBVTT

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.990
They sure aren't making this easy...

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.750
They've got lots of crafty old veterans, too.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.490
Securing these borderlands is no picnic.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.450
And I bet there's still more left to take...

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.000
You even need to ask?

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.470
Look at them down there.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.110
We're in for more of this, and soon.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.560
See?

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.750
Buerger Squad.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.510
We'll make preparations and move out at once.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.450
We have our next mission.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.190
The Price of Smiles

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.190
<i>The Price of Smiles</i>

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:14.020
<b><i>The Ignition of Souls</i></b>

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:29.560
It's time.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.960
Oh? I can finally swap out, huh?

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:37.170
Damn, it's gotten cold.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.080
Want a drink?

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:39.560
It'll warm you up.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.720
Please, it's freezing...

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.140
Hey, is this from your stash?

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.720
Hey, is that alcohol?

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.380
If the commander finds out,
 you'll be in for it.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.230
Oh, chill out.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.670
We're on a mission. Hand it over.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.070
Damn it.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.700
I've known old bastards like him.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.450
Eyes like a hawk, searching around 
for any fault they can find.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.120
But my last commander was all 
about maintaining his pride.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.810
He really kept us at a distance.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.710
I didn't expect it, but this 
type of team has its charms.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.780
Yeah, maybe so.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.320
We've been ordered to stand by for a while.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.150
They said there's a chance our 
moving target might change.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:42.300
How long is "a while"?

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.300
It depends on how the planning meeting goes,

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.350
but I bet they won't reach a decision today.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.160
What the hell?

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.530
So we gotta camp out in this cold?

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.940
Don't worry.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:56.030
We have orders to do maintenance 
on our theurgears while we wait.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.380
By ourselves?!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.720
There's a team of mechanics doing 
the rounds who will offer support.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.010
Our scheduled time frame is 2300 hours.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.330
I get it.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.850
In other words, no time to sleep.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.150
Precisely.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:11.020
Take some free time until 2100.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.070
Sleep or drink, whatever you like.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:16.660
Just make sure you've sobered 
up when the time comes.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.190
This one's cute!

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:22.950
What do you think?

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.660
I... I like it.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.740
Huh? You do?

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.720
You've got weird taste, lady.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.200
That's rude!

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.790
People have always said, 
"Lily, your taste is unique!" in a good way!

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.800
I don't think they meant 
that in a good way...

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.090
H-Hey!

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.110
I'm gonna tell your parents on you!

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.430
You can't.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:52.730
An orphanage?

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:56.460
I don't know if you could 
call it that, exactly...

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.230
There's an elderly couple that's 
letting war orphans live with them.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:05.630
Um... I was wondering if we 
could bring them a pick-me-up.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:09.450
I kind of said something bad...

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.240
Bad?

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:14.250
I said I was gonna tell the kid's parents...

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.370
Is it all right if we go?

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.910
It's a bit far away, but...

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.340
I don't mind.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:24.880
Just see that you're back in time.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:26.820
Thank you, sir.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:29.440
Wait.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:32.680
I'll come, too.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.390
We know it's not much,

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.530
but we hoped it might help you out...

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.830
It might be hard to accept from people

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:45.010
who were your enemies until recently...

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.280
We accept it gratefully.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.610
We truly appreciate your kindness.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.240
Do you look after them all by yourselves?

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:56.150
We didn't intend to, at first.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:00.380
But they just started coming, 
and we couldn't abandon them...

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:06.220
Though, in a way, 
they've ended up looking after us.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.720
But you know things can't 
stay this way forever.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.680
This one's good, right?

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.680
Anja, did you guys draw all of these?

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.240
Yeah, me and the others!

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:22.940
They draw them for fun when it rains.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.090
This picture...

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.780
He drew it.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.950
I've encouraged him to draw other things,

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:37.130
but he always draws the war.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:42.580
I suppose the world he's most 
familiar with these days...

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.230
Hello, there. It's nice to meet you.

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:45.940
What's the matter, now?

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:47.400
Say hello.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:51.480
We were the attackers until recently.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:52.660
It's understandable.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.140
Now, look closer.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.400
You see the trick?

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.770
You can tell he does this a lot!

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:09.770
Yeah.

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:11.030
Hey, hey!

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.990
Let's draw! All together!

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:17.760
Sorry. We can't stay too long.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.410
You can stay a bit longer.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:22.620
Commander?

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:24.040
I'll go back ahead.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.870
Make sure to get some sleep.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.800
Maintenance will have us up all night.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:30.310
Yes, sir.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:33.430
All done!

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:35.430
Who do you think it is?

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:36.770
What are those?

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:37.420
Scary!

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:38.310
Are those people?

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.380
No, they're monsters!

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.070
What did you draw?

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:47.090
It was supposed to be
 the old couple who live here...

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:48.980
I won't tell them if you won't.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:54.490
Kids just don't understand 
my aesthetic sensibilities!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.030
Welcome, weary traveler!

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.290
Have a treat!

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.130
Thank you.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.580
Welcome to Emma's House!

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:07.930
Your name is Emma?

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:08.630
Yeah!

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:11.380
Is this... your house?

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:12.070
Yeah!

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:14.540
I see.

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.600
So this is...

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.840
your place.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.940
Those kids were cute.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:32.740
Yes...

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:37.880
I hope they can make that 
their home forever...

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:41.750
What's wrong?

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:43.250
If...

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:49.460
If you feel like there's nowhere in 
the world where you belong, don't worry.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:52.920
You'll find your place someday.

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:55.680
Did you find a place?

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:57.580
Yes.

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:04.180
I said something like that
 to a child I met before.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.290
I was just trying to comfort her,

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:11.670
but the truth is that, like her,

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.690
I've been searching for 
my place for a long time.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:17.820
There was no place for me with 
the family that raised me.

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:01.370
Hey, you!

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:03.780
You can't stay there.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.120
Do you have a problem with that?

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.440
Just get going.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:32.180
I ended up in the army just to stay alive.

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:34.830
So it's not really my place, either...

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:41.320
Well, I wouldn't say the army
 is my place, either...

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:47.930
But I feel like in this squad, 
with everyone... this is my place.

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:49.620
Everyone?

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.210
Remember Commander Gail before?

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:53.660
"Make sure to get some sleep."

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:55.830
"Maintenance will have us up all night."

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:58.970
He sounded like a fussy old dad.

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:02.000
Don't you think?

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:02.720
Yes.

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:07.940
Warrant Officer Break and 
Guy have their nice sides.

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:13.730
Huey's a jerk, but I think every 
family has their black sheep!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:17.930
Plus I've always wanted a cool big sister!

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:26.740
So I would really like it if you'd 
think of this squad as your place!

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.400
You can't blow me off with 
that expression again!

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:35.050
I'm being serious with you!

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.310
I just...

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:42.320
I'm not sure how to answer you...

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.520
Don't stop working; just listen.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:52.900
We have our next marching orders.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:57.230
We'll meet up with an assault carrier 
120 kilometers to the south,

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:58.900
just outside the State of Leo Tacrath.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:02.530
We'll assault a Royal Army facility, 
to either secure it or destroy it.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.030
Another tough one...

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:08.620
We'll set out at 0630 hours.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:11.400
Finish your maintenance 
within the next two hours.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:17.140
I would really like it if you'd 
think of this squad as your place!

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:19.100
Welcome to Emma's House!

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:23.390
At times like these, you can't 
do much but smile. Right?

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:25.890
Were you one of those children, too?

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.880
Just keep smiling.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:31.300
Smiling will get you through anything.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:36.480
Keep going! Keep going! Keep going!

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.190
Now stop!

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.070
A little more to the right— Hey, stop!

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.150
Are you kidding me?

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:51.290
The mechanics are already gone, right?

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.500
I'm sure we can work it out.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:56.720
The rest of you can go on ahead.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:13:00.080
It'll take about two hours, 
but I'll catch up right away.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:03.550
Of course, you'll be helping me, Stella.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:08.800
It's rare to see you make 
a mistake like this.

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:11.110
I'm sorry.

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:15.060
Well, there's nothing wrong 
with showing a little humanity.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.090
Humanity?

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:19.820
In a way, the battlefield is

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:23.780
where a person most clearly
 shows their true nature.

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:26.690
On the front lines, the toughest man you know

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:29.580
might end up a shrieking, terrified wreck.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:32.910
They can try to keep their calm like you,

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:35.500
but they can't even put up a front.

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:40.100
I'm not... trying to put up a front.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:43.570
That's what I thought, too, at first.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:48.980
I thought you'd left your emotions behind.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.810
But these days...

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:57.920
Do you feel you've changed?

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:02.330
I'm not sure if this way 
is more "you" or not,

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.720
but I think it's a pretty good thing.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.730
Do you think the children we met

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:22.130
will be able to stay like that forever?

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.030
It's a tough question.

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:27.340
It seems impossible for that old 
couple to take care of them alone.

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:30.140
There are many places exactly like that.

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:33.600
We're limited in what we can do for them,

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.720
but something is better than nothing.

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:39.150
Is that why you run an orphanage?

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:40.570
You saw the pictures, right?

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:43.880
I have kids like that in my orphanage, too.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:46.730
Kids who can't draw anything 
but bloody battle scenes.

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:54.200
We're the ones creating kids like that,

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:56.930
so we have a responsibility 
to see them through this.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:02.970
Until the time comes when we can show them 
a different world, a different future...

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.880
Hey, focus on your driving, will you?

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.730
Don't you space out and 
crash into something again.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:11.820
What's wrong?

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:13.940
Lily said something.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:17.100
She said you were like a fussy old dad.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:18.020
What?!

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:20.190
Give me a break...

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.820
I have enough kids as it is.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:38.500
There they are.

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:40.670
We'll join up with them,

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:42.860
then we'll make our way to 
the State of Leo Tacrath.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.450
It's clear! Move!

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:05.660
They're shooting us from pillboxes!

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:07.160
Hold your ground! Return fire!

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:08.280
Take out the machine guns!

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:14.370
That way! Climb that slope!

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:24.000
What the...

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.380
Mines! They've mined part of the slope!

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.880
Get back! Stick to the planned route!

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:36.290
Damn it, they're trying to 
stall us at every turn...

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:39.770
They must be really desperate to 
keep us out of that facility...

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:42.770
What the hell is in there?!

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:44.590
Get back as far as you can!

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:46.020
The carriers are going to start shelling!

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:48.160
They'll destroy the mine field!

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.030
Now! Charge!

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:10.490
<i>You okay, Guy?!</i>

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:14.050
I think so... but my hovers...

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:16.120
Stay there and suck down some booze.

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:17.530
We'll take things from here.

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:21.970
Is everyone all right?

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:23.170
Except for Guy.

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:25.570
He becomes useless at all the worst times.

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:26.440
You said it!

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:37.570
Lily! Behind you!

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:40.330
Damn you!

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:45.510
Get back!

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:51.050
That unit...

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:05.560
Stella!

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:08.520
Commander!

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.030
Commander!

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:28.290
Stay back... it's about to explode.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:31.440
Commander, why...

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.800
Why?

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:35.930
Do I need a reason...

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:39.800
to protect my precious subordinate?

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:41.300
<i>Commander...</i>

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:43.140
Stay back.

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.720
Stella...

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:48.300
Break...

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:50.090
Lily...

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:52.350
Huey...

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:54.600
Guy...

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:58.180
<i>Commander! Commander!</i>

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:04.080
Survive... and see them through...

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:08.270
To the end of the fighting...

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:11.380
And what begins the day after...

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.230
Stella...

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:59.090
Rest in peace before us,

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:02.210
heroic warrior of the Kingdom of Soleil,

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:04.580
Grand Master Harold Miller.

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:06.140
As a token of kindness,

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:12.370
our emperor reaches across the boundary
 that divides friend and foe

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:15.490
to offer his most heartfelt grief.

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:23.070
<i>Ah, the sword you turned against us 
is sheathed one final time,</i>

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:26.730
<i>that you may ascend in peace to the heavens.</i>

00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:30.620
Awfully showy for an enemy funeral.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:31.250
<i>If the times and circumstances 
had not divided us,</i>

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:33.040
That's what they call propaganda.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:34.680
<i>perhaps instead of crossing swords, we 
might have shared a drink as friends,</i>

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:34.850
Propaganda?

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:37.980
<i>and talked of the future of the nations 
to whom we pledged our loyalty.</i>

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:39.410
The Kingdom's as exhausted from 
the drawn-out war as we are.

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:42.720
Playing on their war-weariness 
is a way to undermine them.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:44.100
It's all stupid.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:47.050
Some people didn't even leave a body to bury.

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:54.960
Stella.

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:58.320
Thank you.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.460
Did you know?

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:09.120
The commander wasn't picky,

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:12.220
but beans were the one 
thing he couldn't stand...

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:17.330
Really?

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:21.210
Yes, it's true.

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:30.380
Is that the stuff?

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:31.140
Yeah.

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:41.980
We're on a mission. Hand it over.

00:21:48.170 --> 00:21:51.010
<i>Goodbye... Commander.</i>

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:40.390
<b><i>The Resolve of Two</i></b>
